---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const privacyEmail = 'support@flowmastersuite.com';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Flowmaster handles account, device, trial, diagnostic and AI-feature information, which providers process it, and your privacy rights, including California rights.">
  <article class="privacy-page">
    <header>
      <p class="privacy-label">FLOWMASTER · PRIVACY</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="privacy-intro">This Privacy Policy explains how Flowmaster handles information when you use flowmaster.live, create an account, or use the Flowmaster desktop app and its online services.</p>
      <p class="privacy-date">Effective November 24, 2026 · Last updated November 24, 2026</p>
    </header>
    <div class="privacy-summary"><strong>The essentials</strong><p>Recording, marking, clipping, playback, clean-up and export run on your computer, and account, licence and trial checks never upload your recordings. Cloud AI features (such as Flow AI and cloud transcription) are different: when you use one, the material that task needs is sent through Flowmaster’s online service to a third-party AI provider, which today means Anthropic or ElevenLabs. Crash and fault reports are always sent; usage statistics are off unless you turn them on. We do not sell or share your personal information.</p></div>

    <section aria-labelledby="who"><h2 id="who">1. Who handles your information</h2><p>Flowmaster is provided by Alexander Blair, doing business as Flowmaster (“Flowmaster,” “we,” “us,” “our”), who is responsible for the personal information described in this policy. This policy covers the flowmaster.live website, Flowmaster accounts, the desktop app and its online services (sign-in, licence and trial checks, update checks, diagnostics and AI features), and our administration of accounts, licences and trials. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a>.</p><p>Use of the website and accounts is also governed by our <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>. Use of the installed desktop app is governed by the Flowmaster Desktop App End User License Agreement (EULA) shown in the installer.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="collect"><h2 id="collect">2. Information we receive</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account information.</strong> Your email address, account identifier, verification status, sign-in provider, and account and sign-in timestamps. If you use Google sign-in, we may also receive your name and profile picture. Your password is handled by our authentication provider and is used only to sign you in.</li>
        <li><strong>Release-email preferences.</strong> If you choose to subscribe, we record your account and email address, the consent wording/version and time, and later preference changes. Delivery, bounce, complaint and unsubscribe records help us respect your choices and avoid unwanted messages.</li>
        <li><strong>Device, licence and trial information.</strong> Hashed device identifiers, account-to-device associations, app version, licence assignments and activation/revocation status, trial action counts, reservations, and access or blocking status. Raw hardware serial numbers are not uploaded by the trial identification process. A hardware hash is a persistent identifier, not a guarantee of anonymity.</li>
        <li><strong>Crash and fault reports (always sent).</strong> When the app crashes repeatedly, enters safe mode, rolls back an update, fails an update, or cannot start media protection, it sends a short report: app version (and previous version), crash count, the action taken, a fixed reason code, operating-system version and architecture, a hashed device identifier and, in older builds, the licence key. These reports contain no recordings, file contents or free-text error messages.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage statistics (off unless you opt in).</strong> If you turn on “share usage statistics” in Settings or during setup, the app sends events such as app launches, update checks, saved marks, exports, processed recordings and onboarding steps, with details such as clip counts, durations and step numbers. This setting is off by default.</li>
        <li><strong>AI feature records.</strong> When you use a cloud AI feature, our service records the feature, provider and model used, a hash of the request, token, image and tool counts, credits reserved and charged, and timestamps. These records are used for metering, credit limits, abuse prevention and support. Our service does not store the content of your AI requests or the provider’s answers. See section 4 for what is sent to AI providers.</li>
        <li><strong>Connection information.</strong> Requests to our services and the update feed may record your IP address and timestamps, which we use for security, rate limiting and abuse prevention.</li>
        <li><strong>Communications.</strong> Messages and attachments you choose to send us, and service-message acknowledgments. Diagnostics or support material may contain file paths or other details you include.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="google"><h2 id="google">3. Sign in with Google</h2>
      <p>When you choose “Continue with Google,” Google shares basic identity information with Flowmaster through our authentication provider: your Google account identifier, email address and verification information, and available profile information such as your name and picture. We use it to create or sign into your Flowmaster account, recognize you on later visits, and keep the account secure.</p>
      <p>This sign-in requests basic identity scopes only. It does not request access to your Gmail messages, Google Calendar, Drive files, or contacts. Flowmaster does not receive your Google password. A Flowmaster password you choose separately is for Flowmaster’s password-login screens.</p>
      <p>We do not sell Google user data, use it for advertising targeting, or use it to train AI models. Flowmaster’s use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including its Limited Use requirements.</p>
      <p>You can remove Flowmaster’s access in your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Account connections</a>. Disconnecting Google does not automatically delete your Flowmaster account or existing service records. Contact us to request account deletion.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ai"><h2 id="ai">4. Cloud AI features and AI providers</h2>
      <p>The desktop app includes optional AI features. Some run on your computer. Others run in the cloud: when you use one, the app sends the material that task needs through Flowmaster’s online service (our “LLM proxy”), which forwards it to a third-party AI provider and returns the result. Cloud AI features send material only when you use them. They are not used for account, licence or trial checks.</p>
      <p><strong>Current status:</strong> as of the date above, the cloud AI features are switched off on our service while we finish setting them up, so no material is sent to AI providers yet. This section describes what happens once they are available to you.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Anthropic (Claude language models).</strong> Used by Flow AI and related planning features. Receives your messages and instructions, project and timeline details, transcripts or other text from your project, and still frames or images that the feature includes.</li>
        <li><strong>ElevenLabs (speech-to-text).</strong> Used by cloud transcription and features built on transcripts, such as captions and laughter detection. Receives the audio from the recording or track you choose to transcribe, and any vocabulary terms you add. It returns the words, timings, speaker turns and sound tags such as laughter.</li>
        <li><strong>fal.ai (alternative route for the same speech-to-text model).</strong> Our service can also reach the same ElevenLabs model through fal.ai. When it does, the audio is uploaded to fal.ai’s storage, deleted after the job, and set to expire within one hour in any case. We currently use ElevenLabs directly.</li>
        <li><strong>Google Gemini (experimental scratch narration, off).</strong> An experimental narration feature can send narration text to Google’s Gemini text-to-speech service. It is switched off in normal use and works only with a special launch option and a Gemini API key supplied on that computer.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Providers process this material under their own terms and privacy commitments, which may include keeping it for a limited time for abuse and safety monitoring. Flowmaster does not use your recordings, transcripts or AI requests to train AI models. We may change or add providers; we will update this list when we do. Only submit material you have the right to submit, including any consent the law requires from people whose voices or images appear in it.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="recordings"><h2 id="recordings">5. Your recordings and local files</h2><p>Flowmaster’s recording, marking, clipping, playback, clean-up, event detection and export tools process your files on your computer. Your recordings leave your computer only when you use a cloud AI feature (section 4) or deliberately send files to support. Files you send to support are handled as support material. Third-party applications or services you use alongside Flowmaster, such as OBS Studio or video editors, have their own privacy practices.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="updates"><h2 id="updates">6. Update checks</h2><p>The desktop app checks for updates by downloading a signed update feed and installer files hosted on GitHub (github.com). GitHub receives your IP address and normal request information when this happens, under its own privacy practices. The update check itself does not send your account details or recordings to GitHub.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="purposes"><h2 id="purposes">7. Why we use information</h2><p>We use this information to authenticate accounts, provide recording, editing and AI features, meter AI credits, manage licences, measure and enforce trial allowances, prevent repeated trial resets and abuse, investigate crashes and errors, provide support, send necessary account and service messages, and maintain the security of Flowmaster.</p><p>Authorized administrators can review accounts, associated device activity, trial operations, AI usage records and licensing status to support users and control access. Creating an account or signing in with Google does not subscribe you to release announcements or marketing emails. You can separately choose to receive Flowmaster release announcements and product updates from your account page.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="providers"><h2 id="providers">8. Service providers and disclosures</h2><p>We use these providers to operate Flowmaster:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Supabase</strong> provides account authentication, the database for accounts, devices, licences, trials, diagnostics and AI usage records, and the backend functions, including the LLM proxy. We plan to move the database to <strong>Railway</strong> and sign-in to <strong>WorkOS</strong>; they would then process the same categories of information, and we will update this policy when that happens.</li>
        <li><strong>Anthropic, ElevenLabs and fal.ai</strong> process material you send to cloud AI features, as described in section 4.</li>
        <li><strong>Google</strong> provides optional Google sign-in.</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong> delivers transactional account emails and release updates you choose to receive, receiving the email address and message information needed for delivery.</li>
        <li><strong>GitHub</strong> hosts the public website (GitHub Pages) and the desktop app’s update feed and downloads. <strong>Vercel</strong> hosts our administrative interface. Both process normal hosting and connection information.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We share information with these providers only as needed for the services they perform for us, and for support you request. We may also disclose information when legally required, to protect users and service security, or as part of a business transfer (including to a business entity we form to operate Flowmaster) subject to applicable protections. We do not sell your personal information or share it for cross-context behavioral advertising. Google user data remains subject to the limitations described above.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="website"><h2 id="website">9. The website</h2><p>flowmaster.live does not use advertising cookies, analytics tools or tracking pixels. The site’s fonts and images are served from the site itself. The account page uses your browser’s session storage to keep you signed in within that browser session, and our authentication provider and Google may use their own storage when you sign in. Our hosting provider processes normal connection information, such as IP addresses, to serve the site.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="storage"><h2 id="storage">10. Storage, security, and retention</h2><p>The desktop app stores local settings and the authentication information it needs on your computer. We use access controls and encrypted connections to protect information. No service can guarantee absolute security. Our providers may process information outside your country, including in the United States.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Crash reports</strong> are kept for up to 90 days.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage statistics</strong>, if you opt in, are kept for up to 6 months.</li>
        <li><strong>Audio sent through fal.ai</strong> expires from fal.ai’s storage within one hour. Our service does not keep the content of AI requests or answers; AI providers retain material under their own terms.</li>
        <li><strong>Account, licence, device, trial and AI usage records</strong> are kept while your account is active and as needed afterward to handle support, security, billing and abuse issues, enforce trial and licence limits, and meet legal obligations.</li>
        <li><strong>Email consent history</strong> and limited unsubscribe or delivery-suppression records are kept as needed to honor your email preferences, address delivery problems and demonstrate consent. An unsubscribe does not delete your account or stop necessary account and security messages.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>After an account-deletion request, some restricted device/trial, audit, security, or legally required records may need to remain; backup copies may persist until replaced under the provider’s backup lifecycle. Reinstalling Flowmaster or creating another account does not reset the device trial.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="choices"><h2 id="choices">11. Your choices and rights</h2><p>You can sign out, disconnect Google, leave usage statistics off (or turn them off in Settings), choose whether to use cloud AI features, and choose whether to send support material. You can turn release emails off on your <a href="/account">account page</a> or use the unsubscribe link in a release email. Signing in again does not resubscribe you.</p><p>To request access to, correction of, or deletion of your information, email <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}?subject=Flowmaster%20privacy%20request`}>{privacyEmail}</a>. We may need to verify that you control the account before acting. Do not send us your password, sign-in codes, or API keys. Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights, including rights to object to or restrict some processing or to complain to a privacy authority. We assess requests according to applicable law and explain any information we need to retain. Deleting an account can affect access to Flowmaster.</p>
      <h3>California residents</h3>
      <p>If you live in California, the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act (CCPA/CPRA), gives you the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Know and access</strong> the personal information we have collected about you, its sources, why we use it, and who we disclose it to;</li>
        <li><strong>Delete</strong> personal information we collected from you, subject to legal exceptions;</li>
        <li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate personal information;</li>
        <li><strong>Opt out of the sale or sharing</strong> of personal information. We do not sell or share personal information, including that of anyone under 16, and we treat a Global Privacy Control signal as an opt-out request;</li>
        <li><strong>Limit the use of sensitive personal information.</strong> The only sensitive personal information we handle is your account sign-in credentials, which we use only to sign you in, so there is nothing further to limit; and</li>
        <li><strong>Not be discriminated against</strong> for exercising these rights.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>In the past 12 months we have collected these categories of personal information: identifiers (such as email address, account ID, hashed device identifiers and IP address); customer records (such as account and licence information); internet or electronic activity (such as crash reports, optional usage statistics and AI usage records); and audio, visual or similar information, but only when you use a cloud AI feature. We collect them from you, from your use of the app and website, and from Google if you use Google sign-in, for the purposes in section 7, and we disclose them for business purposes to the service providers in section 8. Retention is described in section 10.</p>
      <p>To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}?subject=California%20privacy%20request`}>{privacyEmail}</a>. You may use an authorized agent; we may ask the agent for proof of authorization and ask you to confirm your identity. We aim to respond within 45 days.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="children"><h2 id="children">12. Children</h2><p>Flowmaster is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a child under 13 has given us personal information, contact us and we will delete it.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="changes"><h2 id="changes">13. Changes to this policy</h2><p>We will update this page when our practices change, including when we add or change AI or infrastructure providers, and revise the date above. Where required, we will provide additional notice or request consent before using information for a new purpose.</p></section>

    <section aria-labelledby="contact"><h2 id="contact">14. Contact</h2><p>Flowmaster (Alexander Blair, doing business as Flowmaster)<br />Website: <a href="https://flowmaster.live">flowmaster.live</a><br />Email: <a href={`mailto:${privacyEmail}`}>{privacyEmail}</a></p></section>

    <div class="privacy-bottom"><a href="/terms">Terms of Service →</a><a href="/account">Your Flowmaster account →</a><a href="/data">More about trial data →</a></div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
